{"type":"message","id":"a57170d5","parentId":"a0c62a7e","timestamp":"2026-07-06T22:58:32.514Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<think>\n1. **Analyze the Request:**\n   - User wants a daily morning and evening news briefing.\n   - Format: 10 news items total (5 from Maeil Business Newspaper, 5 from Korea Economic Daily).\n   - Analysis style: \"Cold/Professional Analyst\" style (WHY, WHAT, HOW, ⚖️ Stakeholders, 💡 Insight) + related links.\n   - Frequency: Twice daily (Morning and Evening).\n   - Tooling: `cron` to schedule the automated briefing.\n\n2. **Identify Necessary Steps:**\n   - Create a cron job to handle this automatically.\n   - The user specified \"10 articles in total (5 MK, 5 HK)\".\n   - Need to set up a `cron` job that triggers at specific times (Morning/Evening).\n   - The user is asking to be \"given\" this service, so scheduling a recurring job via `cron` is the correct path.\n\n3. **Check Constraints:**\n   - Cron schedule: Morning (e.g., 07:00) and Evening (e.g., 19:00).\n   - Agent interaction: `cron add` with a payload.\n   - Payload: Need to ensure the job uses an agent to fetch and analyze.\n\n4. **Drafting the Plan:**\n   - Acknowledge the request.\n   - Explain that I will set up two recurring cron jobs (Morning/Evening).\n   - Use the `cron` tool to schedule these tasks.\n\n5. **Tool Call Formulation:**\n   - Action: `cron add`.\n   - Name: `morning-news-briefing` (6:30 daily).\n   - Name: `evening-news-briefing` (19:00 daily).\n   - Payload: A clear prompt instructing the agent to fetch 5 MK and 5 HK links, analyze them with the requested framework, and send to the user's Telegram ID.\n\n6. **Refinement:**\n   - Wait, the user is currently interacting. I should inform the user that I am setting these up.\n   - The user asked to be \"given\" these, so confirmation of the setup is the best \"final\" action.\n\n7. **Constructing the Final Output:**\n   - \"네, 알겠습니다. 앞으로 매일 아침 6시 30분과 저녁 7시에 신문 기사 10건(매경 5건, 한